# What the root build context must not carry.
#
# The three registry images build from the repository root, because each copies
# a shared module out of backend/ and a service-scoped context cannot see
# outside its own directory. The cost of that is the whole repository being
# sent to the daemon — including 27MB of .git and 212MB of frontend
# node_modules, none of which any image installs. That is slow, and it makes
# every unrelated file a cache-invalidating input.
#
# The frontend and backend images build from their own directories and use
# their own ignore files; this one applies only to the root-context builds.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# 332MB of credentials and installers that must never enter a build context,
# let alone an image layer. Already gitignored; ignored here for the same
# reason, because a root context sends everything the ignore file does not stop.
secrets
**/*secret*
*.dmg
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# Never bake a real environment file into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed, not copied.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite

# Python build and cache artefacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
**/*.egg-info

# Tests do not belong in a production image. `conftest.py` is also the last
# place still indexing a fixed directory depth to find the repository root,
# which is correct where tests run and wrong inside the image.
**/test_*.py
**/conftest.py
**/pytest.ini

# The end-to-end suite needs a live database and three running servers; it does
# not belong in an image.
tests
test_civilization.py

# Documentation and local scratch.
spec
docs
*.md
!services/*/README.md
.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
